#
# Conformance case: foundation/holonic-emergence
# AC: holonic emergence — EmergenceAssessment relative to a reduction theory (issue #705, C2).
#
# Emergence is assessed, never asserted: a logic:EmergenceAssessment over a (whole,
# property, reduction theory) signature receives a tri-valued logic:assessmentVerdict
# the engine DERIVES. One whole (ex:Car, with proper parts ex:Engine, ex:Wheel) and one
# reduction theory (ex:AdditiveTheory, whose logic:reductionBasis carries ex:HasMass but
# NOT ex:Drivable) exercise all three verdicts:
#   * ex:AssessMass  (Car, HasMass, AdditiveTheory) → logic:Aggregate — the theory's basis
#     carries HasMass AND the proper part ex:Engine bears it, so it reduces to the parts.
#   * ex:AssessDrive (Car, Drivable, AdditiveTheory) → logic:Emergent — Car bears Drivable
#     but the theory does not reduce it and no part bears it; reached by negation-as-failure
#     over the aggregate derivation WHILE the theory is still bound, so it is theory-relative.
#   * ex:AssessNuminous (Car, Numinous, NO theory) → logic:EmergenceUnknown — Car bears the
#     property but the assessment declares no reduction theory, so the reducibility question
#     cannot be posed (ME9's first-class third value; failure-to-derive is not irreducibility).
#
# NON-PROPAGATION: no rule propagates logic:bearsProperty down logic:properPartOf, so the
# emergent ex:Drivable stays on ex:Car and never reaches ex:Engine or ex:Wheel — the golden
# materialized.nq contains bearsProperty(Car, Drivable) and properPartOf(Engine/Wheel, Car)
# but visibly OMITS bearsProperty(Engine/Wheel, Drivable). That omission is the non-inheritance
# demonstration, not a gap.
#
# No logic:underMereologyProfile is declared, so weak supplementation stays inert and the
# absence of a logic:WeakSupplementation violation is intentional. The C1 holon-kernel
# co-firings (logic:overlaps, logic:disjoint, logic:hasDisjointCopart) are expected on this
# parthood input and are included — suppressing them would misreport the engine.
#
# CRITICAL: the chase seeds only from input.nq world facts, so all facts below are duplicated
# there in the named world ex:schema; these are the program axioms.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/foundation/holonic-emergence/> .

# Mereology: a car with two proper parts (also world facts in input.nq).
ex:Engine logic:properPartOf ex:Car .
ex:Wheel  logic:properPartOf ex:Car .

# Borne property-values: mass is borne by the whole and by a part; drivability and the
# numinous quality are borne by the whole alone.
ex:Car    logic:bearsProperty ex:HasMass .
ex:Engine logic:bearsProperty ex:HasMass .
ex:Car    logic:bearsProperty ex:Drivable .
ex:Car    logic:bearsProperty ex:Numinous .

# The reduction theory: additive mass reduces to parts; nothing else is in its basis.
ex:AdditiveTheory logic:reductionBasis ex:HasMass .

# Three emergence assessments over the one whole.
ex:AssessMass logic:assessmentWhole ex:Car ;
    logic:assessmentProperty ex:HasMass ;
    logic:assessmentReductionTheory ex:AdditiveTheory .

ex:AssessDrive logic:assessmentWhole ex:Car ;
    logic:assessmentProperty ex:Drivable ;
    logic:assessmentReductionTheory ex:AdditiveTheory .

# No logic:assessmentReductionTheory — the reducibility question cannot be posed.
ex:AssessNuminous logic:assessmentWhole ex:Car ;
    logic:assessmentProperty ex:Numinous .
